# ═══ Draft knowledge entry — CMake on OHOS sysroot: FindBacktrace fallback + test-framework ExternalProject download fix ═══
# Software: g3log 2.4
# Gate: conan-verify G2 (conan create, ohos-aarch64) + local ctest 8/8
# Status: DRAFT — path B candidate, same-stem .md/.kv pair

id: g3log-2.4-cmake-ohos-sysroot
severity: 3
category: cmake|ohos|build-system
trigger_tool: cmake|conan
phase: configure

keywords: FindBacktrace, Backtrace_INCLUDE_DIR, execinfo.h, HarmonyOS, unknown platform, Platform/HarmonyOS, REQUIRED, fallback, CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS, ExternalProject, googletest-download, add_subdirectory, cmake_minimum_required, CMake 4, test framework download

error_signature: Could NOT find Backtrace \(missing: Backtrace_INCLUDE_DIR\)|System is unknown to cmake.*HarmonyOS|add_subdirectory given source .*googletest-src.* which is not an existing directory|Compatibility with CMake < 3\.5 has been removed

match_keywords: FindBacktrace, Backtrace, execinfo, sysroot, OHOS, unknown platform, googletest, ExternalProject, configure-time download, CMake 4, cmake_minimum_required

root_cause: (1) CMake has no Platform/HarmonyOS module, so FindBacktrace's find_path misses the sysroot include even though execinfo.h is on the compiler default include path and backtrace() is in libc; REQUIRED makes configure fail outright. (2) Upstream test bootstrap via ExternalProject can pin an outdated cmake_minimum_required (< 3.5, rejected by CMake >= 4.0) and stale download URLs, making add_subdirectory fail on a missing source dir.

rec_approach: ohos-sysroot-findbacktrace-fallback + fix-externalproject-download-source
rec_description: |
  (1) Downgrade FIND_PACKAGE(Backtrace) to non-REQUIRED; when Backtrace_FOUND is false,
  fall back to the compiler default include search path (execinfo.h) and link libc after
  CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS(c backtrace ""). Keeps symbol detection, only relaxes include-dir
  location on unknown platforms. (2) For configure-time test-framework ExternalProject
  downloads, repair the download source itself (remove stale URLs, bump the download
  project's cmake_minimum_required to >= 3.5) rather than silently disabling tests;
  disabling tests (E342) is the fallback when the source cannot be fixed.
rec_command: |
  # (1) in Build.cmake / CMakeLists.txt:
  #   FIND_PACKAGE(Backtrace)                      # drop REQUIRED
  #   if(Backtrace_FOUND) ... else()
  #     CHECK_LIBRARY_EXISTS(c backtrace "" NEEDS_LIBC_BACKTRACE)
  #     if(NEEDS_LIBC_BACKTRACE) target_link_libraries(<lib> c) endif()
  #   endif()
  # (2) in the ExternalProject download CMakeLists:
  #   cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5)
  #   remove stale URL entries
rec_auto_fix: false

affected_scope: CMake projects that (a) call find_package(Backtrace REQUIRED) and build on OHOS/unknown platforms, or (b) bootstrap a test framework via ExternalProject at configure time with outdated version floors / stale URLs.

verification_cmd: conan create . -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing && ctest --output-on-failure

authors:
  - pc4-4
source_pr:
source_commit:
